[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3816570659","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115564#issuecomment-3816570659","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115564","id":3816570659,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jfD8j","user":{"login":"blueskythlikesclouds","id":19259897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjU5ODk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19259897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds","html_url":"https://github.com/blueskythlikesclouds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-29T09:46:22Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T09:46:22Z","body":"Hm... Looks like this is due to SSR using the last frame for picking the sample, which has fog applied to it. When combined with the reflective surface's own fog, it appears stronger. I'm not sure if there's a good way to fix this one without a deferred renderer.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3816570659/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3817005878","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115564#issuecomment-3817005878","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115564","id":3817005878,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jguM2","user":{"login":"RPicster","id":9423774,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0MjM3NzQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9423774?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RPicster","html_url":"https://github.com/RPicster","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RPicster/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RPicster/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RPicster/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RPicster/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RPicster/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RPicster/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RPicster/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RPicster/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RPicster/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-29T11:15:31Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T11:15:31Z","body":"> Hm... Looks like this is due to SSR using the last frame for picking the sample, which has fog applied to it. When combined with the reflective surface's own fog, it appears stronger. I'm not sure if there's a good way to fix this one without a deferred renderer.\n\nYes, that is the problem.\nI am irritated about it as [I asked for this specific case in the PR of the rework](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111210#issuecomment-3366107946) and it was confirmed that this would fix it.\n\nThis still makes SSR not really useable in any game using fog.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3817005878/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3819189702","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115564#issuecomment-3819189702","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115564","id":3819189702,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jpDXG","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-29T17:32:51Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T17:50:48Z","body":"> Hm... Looks like this is due to SSR using the last frame for picking the sample, which has fog applied to it. When combined with the reflective surface's own fog, it appears stronger. I'm not sure if there's a good way to fix this one without a deferred renderer.\n\nIsn't that the correct behaviour? Reflections should have fog applied from the camera to the point of reflection (the floor) and from the point of reflection to the object being reflected. \n\nThe way I understand it the problem is that the fog in the reflection uses the distance between the object and the camera instead of the distance between the object and the point of reflection (because we are just copying the color from the last frame). So the fog ends up a little bit too strong and may contain lighting information that shouldn't be there. \n\nIn that is the case. Then there is no possibility for volumetric fog to work with SSR. Since the volumetric fog is always aligned with the camera frustum. Even with a deferred renderer, you either use the full fog on your color sample, or you skip fog, but then you end up with not enough fog since you will only have the fog between your eye and the reflective surface and no fog between the surface and the object being reflected. \n\nIt's the opposite problem with the \"correct\" example above. There, it only works because the fog is mostly uniform and the room is small. So the amount of fog between the object and camera is very similar to the amount of fog between the object and floor and between the floor and camera. \n\nThat being said, both Unity and Unreal use basically the same technique for fog, so they must have done something to work around this problem. We might be able to figure out a workaround with some research. I don't think using deferred rendering would help since you still can't take a sample of the fog between the object and the point of reflection","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3819189702/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3820134834","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115564#issuecomment-3820134834","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115564","id":3820134834,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jsqGy","user":{"login":"Saul2022","id":97898580,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdXQVA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97898580?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022","html_url":"https://github.com/Saul2022","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-29T20:26:34Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T20:26:34Z","body":"Maybe  moving The ssr pass before fog could fix it? Don’t know how this stuff works, so take my words with a grain of Salt. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3820134834/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3820395939","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115564#issuecomment-3820395939","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115564","id":3820395939,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jtp2j","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-29T21:18:27Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T21:18:27Z","body":"> Maybe moving The ssr pass before fog could fix it? Don’t know how this stuff works, so take my words with a grain of Salt.\n\nSSR is already calculated before fog","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3820395939/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3823591507","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115564#issuecomment-3823591507","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115564","id":3823591507,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7j52BT","user":{"login":"lander-vr","id":31851431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxODUxNDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31851431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr","html_url":"https://github.com/lander-vr","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lander-vr/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T12:47:42Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T13:20:38Z","body":"If SSR is sampling the previous frame with fog, could a fix be subtracting that frames fog pass from the SSR result?\n\nIf I'm understanding correctly, the sampled reflection color from the previous frame (which includes the fog from that frame) + the fog from that's rendered between the camera and reflection point from the current frame, which we then apply before the current frames fog pass, means we're essentially applying two fog passes to the SSR result.\n\nCould we subtract the fog pass from the SSR result, darkening it? Which then gets brightened back up to the expected color once the current frames fog pass is drawn on top, compensating for fog being applied twice to the SSR result.\n\n<img width=\"1233\" height=\"483\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5901c497-35bf-4ece-a6ce-416fa16ab4ba\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3823591507/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]